<title>JAPAN: Ibiden, Shinko up on prospects for Intel chip.</title>
<headline>Ibiden, Shinko up on prospects for Intel chip.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ibiden Co Ltd and Shinko Electric Industries Co Ltd rose in Thursday morning trade on strong business prospects for those firms which supply components for Intel Corp's latest MMX processor, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0156 GMT, Ibiden was up 60 yen at 1,280 yen, the third most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange in a volume of 2.988 million shares. Shinko was up 170 yen at 4,070 yen.</p>
</text>
